hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22859","Nuh ibn Yazid Abu Muhammad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us: Ibn Ishaq narrated it to me, from Isa ibn Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Faghwa al-Khuzai, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me when he intended to send me with wealth to Abu Sufyan to divide it among Quraysh in Mecca after the conquest. He said: So he said: Seek a companion. He said: So Amr ibn Umayyah ad-Damri came to me. He said: It reached me that you intend to go out and seek a companion. He said: I said: Yes. He said: So I am your companion. He said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have found a companion, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had said: When you find a companion, inform me. He said: So he said: Who? I said: Amr ibn Umayyah ad-Damri. He said: So he said: When you descend on the lands of his people, beware of him, for indeed the speaker said: Your Bakri brother, and do not trust him. He said: So we went out until when I came to al-Abwa, he said to me: Indeed I want something with my people in Waddan, so wait for me. He said: I said: Guided. So when he turned, I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I tightened my camel, then I went urging it on until when I was at al-Asafir, he intercepted me with his clan. He said: And I urged on and outran him. So when he saw that I had escaped him, they left, and he came to me. He said: I had something with my people. He said: I said: Yes. So we went until we came to Mecca, and I handed the wealth to Abu Sufyan."
